  "body": "Stacked on #1076 (on #1070, #1060). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\nNew MCP tool `edit_tool {name, patch}` (`crates/app/src/mcp/tool_edit.rs`, registered in the tools table). `patch` is a partial tool definition in `add_tool`'s `definition` shape, applied as a JSON merge patch over the tool's current definition and run through the existing undoable `ChangeTool` (one undo step), so every ChangeTool gate refuses by tool name (retype stranding an op, bad cutting_data rows, catalog validation, sanity). Unknown keys are refused by name; `number`, `body` and `cutter` are refused by name too (other commands own them; see docs/decisions/1062-mcp-edit-tool.md). Operations on the tool go Stale as with a GUI edit. `lost`/`merge` in `mcp/edit.rs` became `pub(super)` for reuse.\n\n## Tested\n`crates/app/tests/mcp_edit_tool.rs`: `edit_tool_changes_a_field_and_undo_redo_walk_it`, `edit_tool_geometry_marks_operations_stale`, `edit_tool_refusals_name_the_problem` (unknown tool, unknown key, number, bad value, duplicate cutting_data material, non-object patch, retype stranding a Face op). `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/890-cutting-data-per-material` green on the final head; `clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\nBatch/release tiers. The camcraft-mcp skill table is a process file and is not edited here; it should list `edit_tool` (no PROCESS_VERSION bump in this PR).\n\nChangelog: MCP `edit_tool` edits a document tool by partial patch through the undoable ChangeTool.\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1062\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
